WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.394
Hi! How big is a table top? How far is it all the way round? Today we'll learn about area and perimeter, using squares to measure.

2
00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:15.090
Area is how much space is inside a shape.

3
00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:20.634
This rectangle covers 6 squares, so its area is 6 square units.

4
00:00:20.784 --> 00:00:25.002
Perimeter is the distance all the way round the edge of a shape.

5
00:00:25.152 --> 00:00:32.682
This rectangle's perimeter is 3 plus 2 plus 3 plus 2, which is 10 units.

6
00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:38.082
A square with 1 cm sides has an area of 1 square centimetre.

7
00:00:38.232 --> 00:00:45.546
A square with 1 m sides has an area of 1 square metre. We use square metres for a classroom floor.

8
00:00:45.696 --> 00:00:49.530
If there are half squares, two halves make 1 whole square.

9
00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:58.938
6 squares can make a 3 by 2 or a 6 by 1 rectangle. Both have area 6, but different perimeters.

10
00:00:59.088 --> 00:01:07.314
Watch out! Some pupils mix up area and perimeter and write perimeter in square centimetres. That's wrong!

11
00:01:07.464 --> 00:01:15.042
Perimeter is a length, measured in centimetres. Area is the space inside, measured in square centimetres.

12
00:01:15.192 --> 00:01:21.762
Before you write your answer, ask: am I measuring the edge or the inside?

13
00:01:21.912 --> 00:01:32.442
Your turn! A square is 4 squares by 4 squares. What is its area? Pause and think.

14
00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:38.490
4 rows of 4: 16 squares. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:47.010
Another one! What is the perimeter of that square? Pause and think.

16
00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:55.626
4 sides of 4 units: 4 plus 4 plus 4 plus 4 is 16. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:55.776 --> 00:02:06.018
Here's another! 5 whole squares and 2 half squares. What is the area? Pause and think.

18
00:02:06.168 --> 00:02:13.818
2 halves make 1 square. 5 plus 1 is 6 squares. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:13.968 --> 00:02:24.354
Try one more! Should we use square centimetres or square metres for a classroom floor? Pause and think.

20
00:02:24.504 --> 00:02:30.906
A classroom is big, so we use square metres. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:31.056 --> 00:02:40.170
Last one! What is the perimeter of a 5 by 1 rectangle? Pause and think.

22
00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:47.490
5 plus 1 plus 5 plus 1 is 12 units. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:55.962
Remember: area is the space inside a shape, in square units. Perimeter is the distance round it, in length units.

24
00:02:56.112 --> 00:03:01.938
Draw a shape on squared paper and count its area and perimeter!

